Third-party software
====================

This release builds on public packages. Two of them are redistributed in
modified form, as renamed forks under hardware/. Each fork keeps its upstream
license file and carries a NOTICE that records the upstream commit and lists
what was changed. Everything in those two directories remains under the
upstream package's license.

crisp_controllers  ->  hardware/variable_impedance_controllers
  https://github.com/learnsyslab/crisp_controllers
  release 2.4.1, commit ccbead4ba22b1a5b43ac8e81d7137c9ed7b65925
  MIT License. Copyright (c) 2026 Learning Systems and Robotics Lab,
  Technical University of Munich.
  Used as the 1 kHz Cartesian impedance controller. This work adds a log-space
  stiffness rate limiter and an energy-tank passivity guard, and integrates them
  into the Cartesian controller.

franka_ros2_teleop  ->  hardware/fr3_bilateral_teleop
  https://github.com/frankarobotics/franka_ros2_teleop
  commit 69ade0e3e3a344c277f0c159a37ff8bd95c30636
  Apache License 2.0. Copyright 2025 Franka Robotics GmbH.
  Used as the four-channel bilateral teleoperation stack. This work adds payload
  identification, sensorless wrench estimation, compliance label extraction, the
  demonstration recorder and the calibration/validation scripts.

LeRobot
  https://github.com/huggingface/lerobot
  Apache License 2.0. Copyright The HuggingFace Inc. team.
  Provides the SmolVLA backbone. The policy classes under
  src/compliance_vla/policy/ subclass LeRobot's SmolVLA policy and flow-matching
  modules; consult LeRobot's own license for those base classes.

Franka Robotics, FR3 and related marks belong to their respective owners and are
referred to here only to identify the hardware the experiments were run on.
